Subject: notifier, sysupdate: clear "Restart to apply updates" when no backend needs it

A backend notifier announces needsRebootChanged both when a restart
becomes pending and when it is withdrawn, as an image update does when
its staged slot is disarmed in the session. The notifier latches the
first announcement, and the tray item sets its restart title, tooltip
and menu entries once, so a withdrawn restart leaves the tray, and the
persistent "Restart is required" notification, asking for one that
would install nothing. Ask every backend at each announcement, report
the change both ways, close the restart notification when the restart
is withdrawn, and have the tray item follow it both ways.

A withdrawn restart with updates still offered shows the tray item
again at once: the item showed those updates before the install, and
the requiredNotificationInterval wait would hide them until the next
notification time.

The sysupdate backend's updater learns of a restart only from its own
install, and keeps it for the life of the process: an update applied
from a terminal leaves the Updates page saying "Up to date" while the
staged slot waits for a restart, and an open page keeps asking for the
restart after the slot is disarmed. The backend reads io.kdos.Slots1's
State beside sysupdate1 on its bus when it starts and follows it after.
When rebootRequired is true and the armed slot's version (State's
`version` while its `phase` is "armed") is newer than the version the
target's GetVersion answered, less the slot that answer names, it sets the updater's restart; an armed
slot of the running or an older version is a switch between versions
and sets none. When rebootRequired goes false it clears the restart and
reads the targets again, so the page offers the update once more.

